The ONLY existing helper that produces LD-16's exact '2h ago' string. It is a file-local, NON-exported function — not importable as-is. Verbatim:
  function formatRelativeTime(ms: number, nowMs: number): string {
    const deltaS = Math.max(0, Math.round((nowMs - ms) / 1000));
    if (deltaS < 60) return "just now";
    const deltaMin = Math.round(deltaS / 60);
    if (deltaMin < 60) return `${deltaMin} min ago`;
    const deltaH = Math.round(deltaMin / 60);
    if (deltaH < 24) return `${deltaH}h ago`;
    const deltaD = Math.round(deltaH / 24);
    return `${deltaD}d ago`;
  }
Used at line 262: `Last scan {formatRelativeTime(scanStatus.lastCompletedAtMs, Date.now())}`.

miniCards.truncationMechanism:
TWO CSS rules acting together, both in /Users/ozzy/App Development/Loombre/apps/web/src/components/admin/JobsPanel.module.css:

(1) .rowMeta — lines 105-110, verbatim:
  .rowMeta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
    min-width: 0;
  }

(2) .metaItem — lines 112-119, verbatim:
  .metaItem {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-subtle);
    min-width: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }

MECHANISM: `.rowMeta` is a nowrap flex row; each `.metaItem` has default `flex-shrink: 1` plus `min-width: 0`, so when the intrinsic content width exceeds the container the items shrink BELOW their content width and each independently clips + ellipsizes. Because the clipped strings are `created 8/27/2026, 5:59:12 PM` (one continuous run with no break opportunity at the clip point), the ellipsis lands mid-token — e.g. `created 8/27/2026, 5:5…` — which is the mid-word ellipsis LD-16 forbids.

BACKSTOP (not the cause, but why it cannot simply wrap out of the problem): /Users/ozzy/App Development/Loombre/apps/web/src/components/admin/VirtualList.module.css:20-26 sets `.row { position:absolute; inset:0 0 auto; width:100%; overflow:hidden; ... }` and VirtualList.tsx:123 pins each row to `height: rowHeight` (68px, JobsPanel.tsx:34). JobsPanel.module.css:97-104 documents that `flex-wrap: wrap` was REMOVED precisely because a two-line meta row measured 74.2px and painted over the next row. So restoring wrap or adding a line is not available to the lane — the fix must REMOVE content, exactly as LD-16 dictates.

WIDTH MATH AT 1280px (why it bites there and not at 1440+): viewport 1280 -> the `(width <= 1279.98px)` query in AppShell.module.css:103 does NOT match, so the sidebar stays 210px; .main padding-left = 210 + 32 = 242px, padding-right = 32px => 1006px content column (SettingsPageLayout's 1120px cap is not binding). admin/page.module.css:39-44 `.body` is `2fr 1fr` with a 24px gap => right column ≈ (1006 - 24) / 3 ≈ 327px. Minus .collapsibleCard's 2px border, minus .collapsibleBody's 32px horizontal padding (admin/page.module.css:82-84), minus VirtualList .scrollArea's 2px border, minus JobsPanel .row's 32px horizontal padding (JobsPanel.module.css:50) => roughly 259px of usable meta width. Two meta items at 12px (--text-xs) reading `created <full toLocaleString>` and `updated <full toLocaleString>` plus the 16px gap need roughly 315px+ — hence both shrink and both ellipsize.

miniCards.timestampToday:
Produced by ONE file-local helper in /Users/ozzy/App Development/Loombre/apps/web/src/components/admin/JobsPanel.tsx:42-45, verbatim:
  function formatTime(ms: number | null): string {
    if (ms === null) return "—";
    return new Date(ms).toLocaleString();
  }

It is called four times per row — twice for the visible text and twice inside the `title` attributes (JobsPanel.tsx:69-70). `toLocaleString()` with no locale/options argument means the runtime's default locale and format (en-US: `8/27/2026, 5:59:12 PM` — date + time + seconds + meridiem, the longest common form). Job.createdAtMs / Job.updatedAtMs are required non-null int64 ms in the contract (packages/contract/openapi.yaml:7566-7567), so the `"—"` branch is unreachable for these two call sites.

This is the app-wide convention, not a JobsPanel quirk — the same bare `new Date(ms).toLocaleString()` appears at app/admin/sessions/page.tsx:90, components/admin/libraries/StashConnectionPanel.tsx:43, StashSyncPanel.tsx:76, components/admin/system/UpdateNoticeCard.tsx:60, CrashFilesCard.tsx:86, components/admin/settings/ProviderKeysCard.tsx:120, MailCredentialsCard.tsx:164, components/devices/DevicesSection.tsx:64, components/settings/remote-wizard/RemoteDevicesPanel.tsx:52 and PostureCard.tsx:78, app/settings/plugins/[id]/PluginDetailScreen.tsx:543,547, and components/settings/sections/InvitesPanel.tsx:96 / NoticeHistoryPanel.tsx:74. Two admin panels use the shorter `toLocaleTimeString()`: components/admin/StreamsPanel.tsx:143 and components/admin/EventLogPanel.tsx:29.

pinDialog.inputMarkup:
Verbatim from /Users/ozzy/App Development/Loombre/apps/web/src/components/restricted/PinModal.tsx:106-123, including the leading comment block, exactly as it sits between the dots (100-104) and the keypad (125-154):

        {/* Desktop: keyboard-typable numeric field. CSS-hidden on phone,
            where the keypad below is the primary input. Consolidated onto
            the shared ui/Input.tsx TextInput (item 2, Wave A) — inherits
            Input.module.css's `.input:focus-visible` inset ring instead of
            shipping its own copy; PinModal.module.css's `.hiddenInput` now
            only carries the PIN field's own overrides. */}
        <TextInput
          className={styles.hiddenInput}
          type="password"
          inputMode="numeric"
          autoComplete="off"
          autoFocus
          maxLength={PIN_LENGTH}
          value={pin}
          disabled={state.submitting}
          onChange={(e) => setPin(sanitizePinInput(e.target.value))}
          aria-label="PIN"
        />

ATTRIBUTE AUDIT against LD-17's four requirements:
  - inputmode=numeric  — ALREADY PRESENT (line 115).
  - autocomplete disabled — PARTIAL: `autoComplete="off"` is present (line 116), but there is no `autoCorrect="off"`, no `spellCheck={false}`, no `data-1p-ignore`/`data-lpignore`. Note `type="password"` (114) actively invites password-manager fill; `autoComplete="off"` is widely ignored by browsers for password-typed fields. If LD-17's intent is 'no manager/browser autofill', `autoComplete="one-time-code"` or `"new-password"` is the usual stronger form — but that is an interpretation, not what the decision text says, so it needs a ruling rather than a silent choice.
  - aria-label on the input — ALREADY PRESENT: `aria-label="PIN"` (line 122), and PinModal.test.tsx:61 selects on it.
  - focus ring on the dots container — ABSENT. Nothing in PinModal.module.css touches `.dots` on focus; the ring today is Input.module.css:48-52's INSET ring painted on the input's own (currently 160px-wide, visible) box.

Also note: the element renders through `TextInput`, and PinModal.test.tsx:81 asserts PinModal.tsx contains no literal `<input` — so the lane must keep using TextInput and pass any new attributes through its `InputHTMLAttributes` passthrough (Input.tsx:6-9), which forwards everything unfiltered.

The class that will need rewriting, verbatim from PinModal.module.css:63-75:
  input.hiddenInput {
    width: 160px;
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.6em;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-sm);

    /* Deliberately kept distinct from the shared base's --color-surface —
       a translucent fill reads better against SheetOrModal's own raised
       background than the base's solid surface tone does here. */
    background: var(--fill-2);
  }

The name `.hiddenInput` is a MISNOMER today: this field is fully visible at desktop widths (160px wide, monospace, letter-spaced, with a translucent fill and a real border from `.input`). 'Hidden' referred only to the `display: none` mobile branch at lines 131-135. Under LD-17 the name finally becomes accurate.

pinDialog.dotsRendering:
MARKUP — /Users/ozzy/App Development/Loombre/apps/web/src/components/restricted/PinModal.tsx:100-104, verbatim:

        <div className={styles.dots} role="status" aria-label={`PIN entry: ${pin.length} of ${PIN_LENGTH} digits`}>
          {Array.from({ length: PIN_LENGTH }, (_, i) => (
            <span key={i} className={styles.dot} data-filled={i < pin.length} />
          ))}
        </div>

CONTAINER: a plain `<div className={styles.dots}>` — no ref, no tabIndex, no id, not focusable, and NOT associated with the input by `aria-describedby`/`aria-labelledby`. It carries `role="status"` (an ARIA live region, aria-live=polite implicitly) with a dynamic `aria-label` that re-announces on every digit. Note: `role="status"` on a container whose aria-label changes is what makes entry progress audible today; if the lane changes this element it must not silently drop that.

DOTS: exactly PIN_LENGTH (4, from lib/pin-entry.ts:12) empty `<span>` elements, keyed by index, with `data-filled={i < pin.length}` — a real boolean attribute rendered by React as `data-filled="true"` / `data-filled="false"`.

STYLING — /Users/ozzy/App Development/Loombre/apps/web/src/components/restricted/PinModal.module.css:28-47, verbatim:

  .dots {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .dot {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    background: transparent;
    transition:
      background-color var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-out),
      border-color var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .dot[data-filled="true"] {
    background: var(--color-warning);
    border-color: var(--color-warning);
  }

GEOMETRY FOR A RING: `.dots` is 4 x 14px + 3 x 12px gap = 92px wide, 14px tall, with NO padding and NO border-radius of its own — a `--shadow-focus-ring` (0 0 0 3px, tokens.css:219) painted directly on it would hug the 92x14 box tightly and square-cornered. The lane will likely want padding + `border-radius: var(--radius-pill)` on `.dots` (stylelint's declaration-property-value-allowed-list permits `var(--radius-pill)`; a literal px radius would FAIL the gate). `.dots` sits inside `.form` (`display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; gap: var(--space-lg)`), so added padding will not disturb the surrounding layout.

PARENT ORDER inside `<form className={styles.form}>`: (1) `.iconRow` lock glyph, aria-hidden (96-98); (2) `.dots` (100-104); (3) the TextInput (112-123); (4) `.keypad` (128-154); (5) `.error` role=alert, conditional (156-160).

pinDialog.keypadHandling:
MARKUP — PinModal.tsx:128-154. A `<div className={styles.keypad} role="group" aria-label="PIN keypad">` containing, in order: the nine digit buttons 1-9 mapped from `KEYPAD_DIGITS` (line 38: `const KEYPAD_DIGITS = ["1",...,"9"] as const;`), then a `<span aria-hidden="true" />` grid spacer (141), then the '0' button (142-144), then the backspace button (145-153, `aria-label="Backspace"`, containing `<Icon icon={Delete} />`). Total 11 <button> elements — pinned by PinModal.test.tsx:71.

Every key is `type="button"` and `disabled={state.submitting}` (backspace additionally `disabled={state.submitting || pin.length === 0}`).

VALUE PATH — digit press: `onClick={() => appendDigit(digit)}` -> PinModal.tsx:71-74:
  function appendDigit(digit: string): void {
    if (state.submitting) return;
    setPin((prev) => appendPinDigit(prev, digit));
  }
`appendPinDigit` (lib/pin-entry.ts:37-40) no-ops at 4 digits, else `sanitizePinInput(current + digit)`.

VALUE PATH — backspace: `onClick={backspace}` -> PinModal.tsx:76-79: `setPin((prev) => prev.slice(0, -1))`, guarded by `state.submitting`.

KEYBOARD ACTIVATION OF THE KEYS: only the nine digit buttons carry `onKeyDown={(e) => handleKeypadKeyDown(e, digit)}` (line 136). That handler (81-91) calls `event.preventDefault()` and `appendDigit(digit)` on Enter or Space — its own comment (82-86) states this exists so Space never scrolls the sheet and Enter never submits the form, and that it is explicitly NOT a roving-tabindex pattern (plain tab order). The '0' and Backspace buttons have NO onKeyDown, so they rely on native button activation. NOTE the resulting double-fire risk on the digit keys: the handler appends on keydown AND the browser's native click-on-Enter/Space would also fire onClick — `preventDefault()` on keydown suppresses the native activation, which is why it works today; any change here must preserve that.

AUTO-SUBMIT: both paths converge on the single `pin` state, and the effect at PinModal.tsx:54-61 fires `unlock(pin)` the instant `isPinComplete(pin)` is true, guarded by `submittingRef` and clearing the buffer on failure. `state.modalOpen` flipping true clears `pin` (47-49).

VISIBILITY: the keypad is shown at EVERY width — PinModal.module.css:86-91 has no media query and the header comment at 77-85 documents the deliberate H20 decision to stop hiding it above 767.98px. So on desktop the keypad and the text field are BOTH visible today; after LD-17 the keypad becomes the only visible input affordance alongside the dots.

pinDialog.existingVisuallyHiddenUtil:
NO shared/global visually-hidden or sr-only utility class exists in apps/web. Exhaustive grep over apps/web/src for `sr-only`, `srOnly`, `visually-hidden`, `visuallyHidden`, `VisuallyHidden`, `ScreenReaderOnly`, `clip-path`, and `clip: rect` returned exactly ONE hit, and it is a component-scoped CSS-Module class, not a utility:

  /Users/ozzy/App Development/Loombre/apps/web/src/components/ui/Toggle.module.css:14-26, verbatim:

  /* Real checkbox, visually hidden but still hit-testable/focusable/AT-visible
     — the pill below is pure paint, layered via the sibling selector. */
  .input {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

This is the canonical recipe and the exact precedent LD-17 describes — not display:none, not visibility:hidden, still focusable and still in the accessibility tree. Its companion rule at Toggle.module.css:63-65 is the focus-ring transfer:

  .input:focus-visible + .track {
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-focus-ring);
  }

CAVEATS FOR REUSE IN PinModal:
  - It lives in a CSS Module scoped to Toggle, so it cannot be imported by class name. The available mechanisms are (a) copy the eight declarations into `input.hiddenInput`, or (b) CSS Modules `composes: input from "../ui/Toggle.module.css";` — but option (b) would couple the PIN field to the Toggle component's internals and is unprecedented in this codebase for a non-shared class (the only `composes` in apps/web is SheetOrModal.module.css:10, composing from the shared Overlay.module.css). Copying is the conventional choice here; apps/web/src/app/globals.css (the only global stylesheet, 189 lines) currently defines no utility classes at all other than the five `.nf-*` not-found rules at 130-189, so introducing a global `.visually-hidden` there would be a new pattern.
  - The recipe sets `border: 0` and no border-radius; the PIN field currently inherits `border: 1px solid var(--border)` and `border-radius: var(--radius-pill)` from Input.module.css:2-17. Those must be neutralized in `input.hiddenInput`, and per PinModal.test.tsx:93-94 the block must stay a `input.hiddenInput {` compound selector and must NOT contain a `border-radius` declaration inside a bare `.hiddenInput {` block.
  - `position: absolute` with no positioned ancestor: `.form` (PinModal.module.css:9-15) is `position: static`, so the input would position against the nearest positioned ancestor — `overlayStyles.scrim` or `.dialog`. Since it is clipped to 1x1 this is visually inert, but it does remove the input from the form's flex flow (harmless; it currently contributes a 160px-wide row that will simply disappear, tightening the dialog by one `--space-lg` gap).
